# Bare `krowk` prints the overview whether or not a person is at a terminal;
# on a terminal it is the same page, and the flags that once opened the
# agent's screen are refused with a hint to use `-p`. Piped, bare `krowk`
# prints the overview rather than the catalog, which takes --json.
krowk
krowk --json
krowk --format human
@stdin hello\n
krowk
@tty krowk
@tty krowk --json
@tty krowk --resume
@tty krowk --model claude-x
